course: dictionary
lesson: 5040
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «Ink» is a good example. It can be a coloured liquid for writing, or the dark liquid an octopus squirts. Look at the words around it to find the clues.
explain: «Put a white carnation in a glass of water with blue ink: after a day its petals turn blue.» Here ink is a coloured liquid. The clues are the glass of water and the petals turning blue, so the coloured liquid spreads up the stem into the flower.
explain: Ink can also be a verb. To ink something means to put ink on it or to draw over it in ink. Informally, to ink a deal means to sign it. Always ask which meaning fits, then put your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: Context is your best tool when a word has several meanings. Read the whole sentence, look for clues such as glass, petals, octopus or sign, and choose the meaning that fits the story.
fact: Ink is a coloured liquid used for writing, drawing and printing. You find it in pens and printers.
fact: Octopus and squid squirt dark ink to escape from danger.
fact: As a verb, «ink» means to put ink on something or to draw over it in ink.
fact: Informally, to ink a deal means to sign it.
fact: In science, ink is used in chromatography experiments to separate colours, and «ink blot» means a spot of spilt ink.
exercise: «Felt-tip pens have a spongy core soaked in ink.» What does ink mean here? | To sign a deal | A dark liquid an animal squirts | *A coloured liquid for writing and drawing | A kind of paper
exercise: Mia says to ink a deal means to put ink on paper. What does ink a deal really mean? | To spill ink on it | To wash it off | To draw a picture of it | *To sign it
exercise: Which sentence uses ink as a verb? | The octopus squirted ink into the water. | She filled her pen with blue ink. | The ink dried on the page. | *She inked over her pencil sketch in black.
test: «The octopus squirted a cloud of dark ink to escape.» What does ink mean here? | To sign a deal | A kind of paper | *A dark liquid an animal squirts to escape danger | A pen for writing
test: Which phrase means a spot of spilt ink on paper? | inked | *ink blot | ink cartridge | inks
exam: Qi Baishi made a shrimp come alive with a few «ink strokes»: what does ink mean here? | A deal that has been signed | A kind of pencil | A dark squirt to escape danger | *A coloured liquid used for drawing
